<section id="s-roundrobin" data-code="roundrobin">
<div class="section-no">03 — The Round-Robin Key Insight</div>
<h2>Rotate Which Position Each Head Samples</h2>
<p>For a stride of S=4 tokens, there are 4 positions within each stride interval: positions 0, 1, 2, 3. Naive approaches pick the <em>same</em> position for all heads (usually the last). RRAttention rotates: head 0 gets position 3, head 1 gets position 2, head 2 gets position 1, head 3 gets position 0.</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">Sampling Position Formula</div>
  P(i, h) = i·S + (S − 1 − (h mod S))
  <br>
  <span class="math-comment">  i = stride index,  h = head index,  S = stride size</span>
  <br><br>
  Head 0: P(i,0) = i·4 + 3 <span class="math-comment">  ← last position in stride</span>
  <br>
  Head 1: P(i,1) = i·4 + 2 <span class="math-comment">  ← second-to-last</span>
  <br>
  Head 2: P(i,2) = i·4 + 1 <span class="math-comment">  ← second-from-first</span>
  <br>
  Head 3: P(i,3) = i·4 + 0 <span class="math-comment">  ← first position</span>
</div>

<p>The result: every position within a stride is sampled by exactly one head. Across all heads, <strong>full coverage is achieved</strong> — without any single head ever mixing distributions from multiple queries.</p>

<!-- Interactive Round-Robin Canvas -->
<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">round-robin sampling — stride S=4, 4 heads</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">click a head to see its samples</span>
  </div>
